 - Phase ports and compressor (phase-ports batch): a fluid tank's pipe ends are phase ports by face (top = gas outlet, bottom = liquid outlet, sides = bulk as before, inflow through any face undistinguished), and every port draws its vessel's phases by priority, each up to what the vessel held at the step start and the next phase with the rest within the same step (bottom: heaviest liquid, lighter liquid, then gas; top: gas, then the lighter and the heavier liquid; decision D11, replacing an absent-phase closure that never shipped), with the transported stream, reconstruction booking, pipe transfer and solid mobility read per end; a level head `g m_c H / V` (H = 1 m) at every bottom port's driving pressure (D9); the centrifugal pump is liquid-only: a pump whose suction delivers more than 2 % vapour by volume is closed with the typed endpoint mode `INLET_WRONG_PHASE` and its reason on the status line, decided once per 5 s slice with hysteresis (resume below 0.5 %), the island keeps running; a new gas compressor block (`fluid_compressor`, "Process Gas Compressor") with a suction-flow target, a pressure-ratio limit `(r_max - 1) P_suction` (ratio 1.01-10, default 3) and ideal isothermal work booked as heat into the discharge, refused on more than 1 % condensed by mass or any solid; generators are one-way from the cold start (a one-way pressure estimate closes receiving generator runs before the cold rate seed's first pass, D12); a step the reconstruction's equation gate refuses is polished once on a fresh Jacobian before it is refused (D13); a dry-seeded junction with water reachable gets a 1e-12 water trace in its seed (D10); tank page "Connections by face" with what each outlet drew and the level head, compressor page with the ratio field; **checkpoint format 6 (pipe ports, compressor control), breaking, fresh world**; wire protocol fluid-7; new gate tests `PhasePortTest`, `PhasePortPriorityTest`, `LevelHeadTest`, `JunctionWaterTraceTest`, `VentGatePolishTest`, `Inlet